I'll analyze this commit to provide feedback and extract learnings.

## Code Review

```json
{
  "summary": "This commit removes the 'type' column from task INSERTs and fixes a minor SQL syntax (adds ::uuid cast), but contains a CRITICAL BUG: parseInt radix is 3 instead of 10 in AgentSessionService.ts:24.",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "parseInt usage",
      "reminder": "Always use radix 10 as the second argument to parseInt: parseInt(value, 10). The radix parameter defines the number base (3=ternary), not a default value."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Database migrations",
      "reminder": "When removing a column from INSERTs, ensure the column is nullable or has a default in the database schema, or run a migration first to avoid runtime errors."
    },
    {
      "topic": "SQL type casting",
      "reminder": "PostgreSQL uses :: for type casting ($1::uuid), not $1 alone. This is correct in the commit."
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "critical",
      "file": "src/services/AgentSessionService.ts",
      "line": 24,
      "description": "parseInt uses radix 3 instead of 10. This will cause incorrect session limits (e.g., '10' becomes 1 in base 3).",
      "fix": "Change parseInt(process.env.NEZHA_MAX_SESSIONS ?? '3', 3) to parseInt(process.env.NEZHA_MAX_SESSIONS ?? '3', 10)"
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/cli/index.ts, src/services/MeetingHandler.ts, src/services/ReviewService.ts",
      "description": "The 'type' column is removed from INSERTs. If the column still exists in the database schema as NOT NULL, these queries will fail at runtime.",
      "fix": "Verify the tasks table schema allows NULL for the type column, or run a migration: ALTER TABLE tasks ALTER COLUMN type DROP NOT NULL;"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Add integration tests for AgentSessionService to verify session limits work correctly",
    "Consider adding a database migration script rather than silently removing column references",
    "The diff shows arrow function was simplified from (item) => ({ to item => ({ - this is good style simplification"
  ],
  "praise": "Good SQL improvement with ::uuid type casting. Good removal of unused 'type' parameter which simplifies the codebase. Clean arrow function simplification.",
  "overallScore": 40,
  "codeQualityScore": 50,
  "testCoverageScore": 30,
  "documentationScore": 60
}
```

**Critical Fix Needed**: The `parseInt` bug on line 24 of `AgentSessionService.ts` will cause session limits to be parsed incorrectly (e.g., "10" becomes 1 in base-3). This needs immediate attention.

